    <tags>calendar appointments icalendar ics encrypted sqlite portable</tags>
    <summary>Encrypted calendar for Windows. No account, no sync, no telemetry.</summary>
    <description>Free and open-source calendar for Windows with no account, no sync and nothing phoning home. Your appointments live in a single .kcal file on your own machine, an ordinary SQLite database until you put a password on it. Install or run portable.

- Four views, month, week, day and agenda, with one shared previous / next / today control; month zooms from one to six visible weeks and draws multi-day appointments as continuous runs
- Appointments edited in a slide-out sidebar panel rather than a dialog: title, start and end, all-day, location, description and attendees
- Repeating appointments, daily, weekly on the days you tick, monthly or yearly, every N of those, ending never, after a count or on a date, with per-date exceptions; editing or deleting one date asks whether you mean that date or the whole series
- Drag to move appointments across times and days; overlapping appointments sit side by side instead of hiding one behind the other
- Color categories you define, painting every view, plus a 5-day work week toggle and a grid density control down to quarter hours
- Import and export in the formats people actually hand you: iCalendar (.ics, RFC 5545) both ways, CSV in Outlook's column format both ways, saved email invites (.eml) in, and a themed month-by-month web page out with a print stylesheet
- Optional encryption: the lock button puts a password on a Killendar and encrypts it at rest with SQLCipher (AES-256, per-page HMAC-SHA512); opt-in, so no password means a plain readable SQLite file
- As many Killendars as you like, work, on-call, family, each its own .kcal file with its own password or none, kept in the default profile folder, another folder you choose, or beside the portable executable
- Thirteen themes including a full 98SE recreation; Dark, Light, Black and 98SE each carry six accent colors for 33 looks in all
- Localized in fifteen languages, switchable without a restart
- Keyboard driven with single-key shortcuts and a full shortcut overlay on F1, with list and visual keyboard views
- Verified code signing shown in the About card, checked with WinVerifyTrust rather than read off the file
- One self-contained Windows EXE, no runtime install; runs portable, self-installs per-user without UAC or machine-wide with /silent for scripted deployment, and uninstalls without deleting your appointments
- GPLv3, local-only, no account, no telemetry
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/SteveTheKiller/Killendar/releases/tag/vREPLACE_VERSION</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
